title A park is not a landing, and the box it certified held a whole feature
prompt The baton, unattended lap 4079 on grain-patchouli. Rota row 4 by count (Earth, the concrete), taken as counted -- every row had already been read today by some ship, so there was nothing to advance past.
think Earth reads the concrete fact at the door before any argument about it. So I opened by reading what was actually in front of me rather than what the card said was next, and the first concrete thing was git stash list: three stashes, from three dead laps, none of them opened.
think stash@{0} held six files that stand nowhere in this tree -- Weave.annotate, its 377-line Rye witness, a head scan, a control, a Rishi runner, a roster line. 1,107 insertions. My own lane, already proven GREEN on a lap that never sent. The card names annotate as my next real work and it was already written.
think So the honest question was not whether to write it again but why nothing had said it was there. tools/f/stash_record_witness.rish is rostered tier lap and exists for exactly this; it read unlanded=0 verdict=ok on the same tree, the same hour.
think Its answer named the reason: landed:refs/heads/pier/diverged-20260906-131810. The record IS carried by a ref -- a park branch, which is the round open's other dead-letter box. The guard built for the first drawer accepted the second as proof the first was empty.
think Both rows are already booked and both are right about their own drawer. %464 built the reader for the stash; %499 measured the park -- 11 branches on xy, 33 subjects, ten no hand ever brought home. Neither reached the seam, and the seam is where a guard reads one as the cure for the other.
think I measured before repairing, with the record moved off disk so the refs alone answer. Elder: landed:refs/heads/pier/..., unlanded=0, verdict=ok. Repaired: unlanded:parked:refs/heads/pier/..., unlanded=1, parked=1, verdict=records_unlanded. It is carried by no reader ref at all -- not main, not xy/main. 23 park refs stand on this tree.
think The exclusion follows the NAMESPACE rather than the diverged- prefix, because fleet_round_open.sh writes pier/rebase-<stamp> there too and its own header calls refs/heads/pier/ the rota's deferral shelf. A park named something else tomorrow is still a park.
obs ONE GATE, ONE DIAGNOSIS, AND THAT CHOICE KEPT THE REPAIR INSIDE MY OWN SEAT. unlanded stays the single gate and keeps its meaning -- a record no reader ref carries -- with parked reported as the subset a park does carry. Two readings that always fire together are one reading wearing two names. It also means fleet_round_open.sh is untouched: it greps ^unlanded= and starts printing correctly on its own, so six ships get the true reading with no edit across a seat boundary (%291).
obs THE CONTROL'S NEW LEGS WERE PROVEN BY BREAKING THE SCAN, NOT BY WATCHING THEM PASS. 22 legs to 34, and running the grown control against HEAD's scan bit 8 of them -- including both negatives. A refusal proven only in the passing direction cannot be told from a bypass, and I had just watched that exact failure in the file.
obs A RIDER FOUND THE SAME WAY. My first draft's needles read 060606<TAB>unlanded and matched nothing, because a line is <stash><TAB><path><TAB><state> and the stamp sits inside the path. Then I looked at leg 21, written months before mine, and it carried the identical shape: nk "and is not called unlanded" "050505<TAB>unlanded" -- a negative assertion that could never fire, passing for the wrong reason since the day it was written. Anchored on the basename now, and it bites.
obs AND ONE ASSERTION I WROTE COULD NOT BE REACHED EITHER. The welcome leg wanted verdict=ok after moving the record off the park, and the pen deliberately holds an unlanded record from leg 19, so that number is unreachable from there. A welcome asserted on a number the pen cannot reach proves the pen. It asserts the record's own line and parked=0 instead, and says why in the comment.
obs THE PARKED WORK ALSO CLOSED A RED THAT WAS STANDING ON THE ROSTER. The cold open read standing_equipment red on unrostered: mantra_weave_annotate -- the run card carried a receipt for a guard the roster did not name, because the roster line rode in the same stash. Landing the work took runs_unrostered 1 -> 0. The two remaining reds are sow_allow_reach, the seed gate, and the guard's own self-record.
obs THE NUMBER MOVED FOUR TIMES AND THE STAMP DID NOT. The recovered row was booked %485 on 20260906.115458; a peer took %485 while it sat parked, then %501 and %502 landed upstream between my fetch and my write, then %503 on the first rebase, then %504 and %505 on the third -- both of those in the PIN rather than on a shelf, so a shelf-name check missed them and only the merge conflict showed it. It is %506 now and its stamp is unchanged, which is the derived spine working exactly as written: the key is the stamp, the number is a view the anointed remote allocates. Four firings of the same question in one send.
obs I APPLIED THE STASH RATHER THAN POPPING IT, ON PURPOSE. The scan's own doctrine is that the only way to turn it green is to put the record back in the channel and never to drop the stash, and this tree now demonstrates that rather than asserting it: the box still holds three stashes and the reading is green because the record landed.
obs TWO GUARDS BIT MY OWN NEW FILES BEFORE THE SEND, AND BOTH WERE RIGHT. rye_witness_walker went 119 to 120 over a ceiling of 119, because a witness that only CALLS its module leaves every uncalled declaration unanalyzed -- the %463/%470 finding. Four comptime lines fixed it and made the GREEN cover what the module publishes rather than what I happened to call; walked 2 -> 3, unwalked back to 119. Raising the ceiling was the other door and it is a ratchet turned backwards. And fold_shelf_link caught four links in the account I folded, still reading archive/X from inside construction/archive -- %474's exact shape, caught on the lap it arrived.
obs NAMED RATHER THAN FIXED: construction/archive stands at 300 flat against the 256 bound, and three of those are mine. It is an UNDATED room, so the meter reports it (undated_over=1) and gates nothing -- a fold there wants a resolver for basenames carrying no stamp, which is a lap rather than a line.
