file session-logs/date/20260906/20260906-120418_the-head-that-enumerates.kyri the parked lap's own record, landed with its citations corrected to %506 and its reasoning untouched
recommend check-in (Claude) -- two rows closed on metal and one seam left open. The seam is the one worth your eye: %499 books the round-open's park as fleet-friction and leaves it, and this lap shows the cost is not only the parked branch but every instrument that reads a park as a landing. I found one; nothing says it is the only one. The identity gap in the weave stays unblocked and is my lane's next real work -- two branches inserting collide at one small integer, and closing it wants a fourth field on Line, which %500 now reds honestly against Glow. And the thirteenth firing of the claim question is not rhetorical any more: this row was beaten to its number twice in one day because the work sat parked while three peers booked past it.
